.policy "tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn" revision 1
.description "A TanStack Query queryFn that runs on the client must not be or call a Server Action from a 'use server' module; fetch through a Route Handler and keep Server Actions for mutations."
.language typescript
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.ts", "**/*.mts", "**/*.cts", "**/*.tsx", "**/*.js", "**/*.jsx", "**/*.mjs", "**/*.cjs"
.scope exclude "**/*.test.*", "**/*.spec.*", "**/*.cy.*", "**/__tests__/**", "**/test/**", "**/tests/**", "**/e2e/**"
.scope exclude "**/__mocks__/**", "**/*.stories.*", "**/*.story.*", "**/__stories__/**", "**/__fixtures__/**"
.scope exclude "**/fixtures/**", "**/node_modules/**", "**/dist/**", "**/build/**", "**/out/**", "**/.next/**"
.scope exclude "**/coverage/**", "**/vendor/**", "**/.venv/**", "**/.yarn/**", "**/generated/**", "**/__generated__/**"
.scope exclude "**/*.generated.*", "**/*.gen.*", "**/*.min.js", "**/*.d.ts"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. A Server Action (a function exported from a module that starts with 'use server')
// called from the browser is a POST that Next.js runs one at a time per client. React Query runs queries in
// parallel and refetches them on focus, mount and invalidation, so a query whose queryFn is an action queues behind
// every other action call and can stay pending or never run; passed by reference, the action also gets React Query's
// QueryFunctionContext (an AbortSignal), which cannot be serialised and throws. The TanStack docs and React both say
// to keep Server Functions for mutations. It reports, in a file that imports TanStack Query and whose package (its
// nearest package.json) depends on `next`, the action inside a `queryFn` (a `queryFn:` property, a `queryFn() {}`
// method, or the shorthand `{ queryFn }`); a Vite or React Router app with an `app/` folder is not Next.js:
//   queryFn: getProjects                               reported: the action by reference
//   queryFn: () => getProjects()                       reported: a call anywhere in the function's body
//   queryFn: async () => actions.getProject(id)        reported: through `import * as actions`
//   queryFn: () => listProjects()                      reported: an index.ts that re-exports the action
//   queryFn: loadProjectCount                          reported: a workspace function (this file's or an imported
//                                                      one) whose own body references an action, one call deep
//   queryOptions({ queryKey, queryFn: () => getProjects() })    reported: options a client hook will use
//   usePrefetch() { … queryClient.prefetchQuery({ queryFn: () => getProject(id) }) }   reported: in a `use*` hook
// Near misses it leaves alone:
//   useMutation({ mutationFn: createProject })         not reported: mutations are what actions are for
//   await queryClient.prefetchQuery({ queryFn: () => getProjects() })  in a Server Component (no 'use client', not
//                                                      in a `use*` function): on the server it is a plain call
//   queryOptions(…) in a module that imports 'server-only', or in a 'use server' module: never on the client
//   queryFn: fetchProjectsFromApi / () => fetch('/api/projects')        not reported: no action
//   RTK Query's `build.query({ queryFn })` in a file without a TanStack Query import: not this library
//   test and story files (scope)
// Gaps: an action that reaches the queryFn as a prop or a function argument (`useQueryFactory(listAction)`) is not
// seen; helpers are followed one call deep; a `'use server'` barrel that re-exports plain functions, and inline
// `'use server'` functions (only Server Components can define them, and they reach clients as props) are not seen.
// A prefetch in a component file without 'use client' (an event handler) counts as server code. An import is followed
// only where tsx/names resolves it: a relative path, or an alias (`@/`, `~/`, `#/`) the tsconfig's `paths` map.

#include "tsx/modules.rerail"

.violation ServerActionQueryFn(at: node, x: symbol, p: symbol)
    "This `queryFn` runs `{x}`, a Server Action from the 'use server' module {p}. Next.js runs Server Actions one at a time, while React Query runs queries in parallel and refetches them, so this query queues behind other actions and can stay pending; passed by reference, the action is also sent React Query's AbortSignal, which cannot be serialised. Read the data through a Route Handler (`app/api/…/route.ts`) that calls the same server code and `fetch` it here, or load it in a Server Component and pass it down; keep Server Actions for mutations (`useMutation`). If this query only ever runs on the server (a prefetch in a Server Component), leave it."
ServerActionQueryFn(n, x, p) :- saqf_client_fn(v), saqf_part(v, n), saqf_sym(n, q), saqf_action(q, x, p), docof(n, d),
    saqf_next_doc(d).

.violation ServerActionViaHelper(at: node, g: symbol, x: symbol, p: symbol, ol: number)
    "This `queryFn` runs `{g}`, which calls `{x}` ({p}:{ol}), a Server Action from a 'use server' module. Next.js runs Server Actions one at a time, while React Query runs queries in parallel and refetches them, so this query queues behind other actions and can stay pending. Have `{g}` read the data through a Route Handler (`app/api/…/route.ts`) that calls the same server code, or load it in a Server Component and pass it down; keep Server Actions for mutations (`useMutation`). If this query only ever runs on the server (a prefetch in a Server Component), leave it."
ServerActionViaHelper(n, g, x, p, ol) :- saqf_client_fn(v), saqf_part(v, n), saqf_helper_key(n, hk),
    saqf_helper_first(hk, x, p, ol), text(n, g), docof(n, d), saqf_next_doc(d).

// saqf_next_doc(d): document d's package (its nearest package.json; the workspace root's for a file under no other)
// depends on Next.js, whose Server Actions run one at a time. An `app/` folder is no proof: React Router, Remix and
// Vite apps use one too, and a 'use server' module outside Next.js is not this runtime.
.decl saqf_next_doc(d: number)
saqf_next_doc(d) :- doc(d, f, _), package_for(f, dir), saqf_dep_list(l), package_field(dir, cat(l, "/next"), _).
.decl saqf_dep_list(l: symbol)
saqf_dep_list("dependencies"). saqf_dep_list("devDependencies"). saqf_dep_list("peerDependencies").

// ---- TanStack Query and its queryFn ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// saqf_tq_doc(d): d imports @tanstack/react-query, @tanstack/query-core, another @tanstack/*-query package or v3's
// react-query.
.decl saqf_tq_doc(d: number)
saqf_tq_doc(d) :- import_spec(i, s), docof(i, d),
    match("@tanstack/([a-z]+-)?query(-[a-z-]+)?(/.*)?|react-query(/.*)?", s).
// saqf_fn(o, v): object o, in a TanStack Query file, has a queryFn v: `queryFn: v`, `queryFn() {}` (v the
// method), `{ queryFn }` (v the shorthand name).
.decl saqf_fn(o: node, v: node)
saqf_fn(o, w) :- kind(pr, "pair"), field(pr, "key", k), text(k, "queryFn"), field(pr, "value", v), deparen(v, w),
    child(o, pr, _), kind(o, "object"), docof(o, d), saqf_tq_doc(d).
saqf_fn(o, m) :- kind(m, "method_definition"), field(m, "name", k), text(k, "queryFn"), child(o, m, _),
    kind(o, "object"), docof(o, d), saqf_tq_doc(d).
saqf_fn(o, s) :- kind(s, "shorthand_property_identifier"), text(s, "queryFn"), child(o, s, _), kind(o, "object"),
    docof(o, d), saqf_tq_doc(d).

// saqf_client_fn(v): queryFn v can run in the browser: every queryFn but one in server code (saqf_server_site).
.decl saqf_client_fn(v: node)
saqf_client_fn(v) :- saqf_fn(o, v), !saqf_server_site(o).
// saqf_server_site(o): the options o sit in server code: a file without 'use client' that imports 'server-only'
// or starts with 'use server', or a prefetchQuery/fetchQuery/ensureQueryData/… argument outside any `use*` function.
.decl saqf_server_site(o: node)
saqf_server_site(o) :- saqf_fn(o, _), docof(o, d), !saqf_directive_doc(d, "use client"), saqf_server_doc(d).
saqf_server_site(o) :- saqf_fn(o, _), docof(o, d), !saqf_directive_doc(d, "use client"), saqf_prefetch_arg(o),
    !saqf_in_hook(o).
.decl saqf_server_doc(d: number)
saqf_server_doc(d) :- saqf_directive_doc(d, "use server").
saqf_server_doc(d) :- import_spec(i, "server-only"), docof(i, d).
.decl saqf_directive_doc(d: number, x: symbol)
saqf_directive_doc(d, x) :- program(d, p), directive(p, _, x), (x = "use client" ; x = "use server").
.decl saqf_prefetch_arg(o: node)
saqf_prefetch_arg(o) :- kind(c, "call_expression"), field(c, "function", f), kind(f, "member_expression"),
    field(f, "property", pr), text(pr, m), saqf_prefetch(m), field(c, "arguments", a), child(a, o, _).
.decl saqf_prefetch(m: symbol)
saqf_prefetch("prefetchQuery"). saqf_prefetch("fetchQuery"). saqf_prefetch("ensureQueryData").
saqf_prefetch("prefetchInfiniteQuery"). saqf_prefetch("fetchInfiniteQuery"). saqf_prefetch("ensureInfiniteQueryData").
// saqf_in_hook(o): o is inside a function named like a hook, `function useX()` or `const useX = () => …`.
.decl saqf_in_hook(o: node)
saqf_in_hook(o) :- saqf_prefetch_arg(o), inside(o, f, saqf_fn_kind), saqf_fn_name(f, x), match("use[A-Z0-9].*", x).
.decl saqf_fn_name(f: node, x: symbol)
saqf_fn_name(f, x) :- kind(f, "function_declaration"), field(f, "name", n), text(n, x).
saqf_fn_name(f, x) :- kind(v, "variable_declarator"), field(v, "value", f), saqf_fn_node(f), field(v, "name", n),
    kind(n, "identifier"), text(n, x).

// ---- what the queryFn names ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl saqf_fn_kind(k: symbol)
saqf_fn_kind("arrow_function"). saqf_fn_kind("function_expression"). saqf_fn_kind("function").
saqf_fn_kind("method_definition"). saqf_fn_kind("function_declaration"). saqf_fn_kind("generator_function").
saqf_fn_kind("generator_function_declaration").
.decl saqf_fn_node(f: node)
saqf_fn_node(f) :- kind(f, k), saqf_fn_kind(k).
.decl saqf_type_kind(k: symbol)
saqf_type_kind("type_query"). saqf_type_kind("type_annotation"). saqf_type_kind("type_arguments").
// saqf_part(v, n): n is queryFn v itself (a name), or a name or namespace member in v's body, outside types.
.decl saqf_part(v: node, n: node)
saqf_part(v, v) :- saqf_client_fn(v), !saqf_fn_node(v).
saqf_part(v, n) :- saqf_name(n), inside(n, v, saqf_fn_kind), saqf_client_fn(v).
.decl saqf_name(n: node)
saqf_name(n) :- kind(n, "identifier"), !inside(n, _, saqf_type_kind), !field(_, "object", n).
saqf_name(n) :- kind(n, "shorthand_property_identifier").
saqf_name(n) :- kind(n, "member_expression"), field(n, "object", o), kind(o, "identifier"), ns_target(o, _).
// saqf_sym(n, q): n denotes symbol q ("module#name"): an imported name tsx/names resolves (a relative path, or an
// alias the tsconfig's `paths` map) and follows through re-exports (tsx_names__exports), a namespace member
// `actions.getProject`, or a top-level name of n's own file.
.decl saqf_sym(n: node, q: symbol)
saqf_sym(n, q) :- (kind(n, "identifier") ; kind(n, "shorthand_property_identifier")), saqf_imported(n, q).
saqf_sym(n, q) :- kind(n, "member_expression"), field(n, "object", o), ns_target(o, t), field(n, "property", pr),
    text(pr, x), tsx_names__exports(t, x, q).
saqf_sym(n, @qname(m, x)) :- (kind(n, "identifier") ; kind(n, "shorthand_property_identifier")), ref_site(n, site),
    top_level(site, x), docof(n, d), ts_module(d, m).
// saqf_imported(n, q): the name n is imported, and denotes the symbol q.
.decl saqf_imported(n: node, q: symbol)
saqf_imported(n, q) :- ref_site(n, sp), import_binding(sp, _, s, x), x != "*", docof(n, d), target(d, s, t),
    tsx_names__exports(t, x, q).
// saqf_server_name(q, x, p): q is the name x declared at the top of, or exported by, the 'use server' module in file
// p. Each such file states its own; saqf_action reads every file's.
.decl saqf_server_name(q: symbol, x: symbol, p: symbol)
saqf_server_name(@qname(m, x), x, p) :- saqf_directive_doc(d, "use server"), ts_module(d, m), doc(d, p, _),
    saqf_own_name(d, x).
.decl saqf_own_name(d: number, x: symbol)
saqf_own_name(d, x) :- top_level(site, x), docof(site, d).
saqf_own_name(d, x) :- kind(e, "export_statement"), exported_decl(e, x), docof(e, d).
// saqf_action(q, x, p): symbol q is x, of the 'use server' module in file p. Across files, by symbol.
.decl saqf_action(q: symbol, x: symbol, p: symbol) cross_file
saqf_action(q, x, p) :- saqf_server_name(q, x, p).

// A helper is keyed by its symbol where it is declared at the top of a module (this file's or an imported one's), and
// by its file's path and its line and column where it is declared in a narrower scope of the queryFn's own file.
// saqf_helper_key(n, hk): name n in a queryFn denotes the helper keyed hk.
.decl saqf_helper_key(n: node, hk: symbol)
saqf_helper_key(n, hk) :- saqf_client_fn(v), saqf_part(v, n), saqf_sym(n, hk).
saqf_helper_key(n, hk) :- saqf_client_fn(v), saqf_part(v, n), ref_site(n, site), !top_level(site, _),
    saqf_site_fn(site, h), saqf_fn_key(h, hk).
// saqf_fn_key(h, hk): function h, declared at site, is keyed hk.
.decl saqf_fn_key(h: node, hk: symbol)
saqf_fn_key(h, @qname(m, y)) :- saqf_site_fn(site, h), top_level(site, y), docof(site, d), ts_module(d, m).
saqf_fn_key(h, cat(p, ":", to_string(l), ":", to_string(c))) :- saqf_site_fn(site, h), !top_level(site, _),
    line(h, l), col(h, c), docof(h, d), doc(d, p, _).
.decl saqf_site_fn(site: node, h: node)
saqf_site_fn(f, f) :- kind(f, "function_declaration").
saqf_site_fn(s, f) :- kind(s, "variable_declarator"), field(s, "value", f), saqf_fn_node(f).
// saqf_helper_name(hk, q, p, l, c): in its own body, the function keyed hk, of a file that is no 'use server' module,
// names the imported symbol q at line l, column c of the file at path p. Only an imported name can be another
// module's action: this file's own top-level names are no 'use server' module's.
.decl saqf_helper_name(hk: symbol, q: symbol, p: symbol, l: number, c: number)
saqf_helper_name(hk, q, p, l, c) :- saqf_fn_key(h, hk), docof(h, d), !saqf_directive_doc(d, "use server"),
    saqf_name(y), inside(y, h, saqf_fn_kind), (saqf_imported(y, q) ; kind(y, "member_expression"), saqf_sym(y, q)),
    line(y, l), col(y, c), doc(d, p, _).
// saqf_helper_first(hk, x, p, l): the first name in helper hk's own body that denotes an action, x, is at line l of
// the file at path p.
.decl saqf_helper_hit(hk: symbol, q: symbol, p: symbol, l: number, c: number) cross_file
saqf_helper_hit(hk, q, p, l, c) :- saqf_helper_name(hk, q, p, l, c), saqf_action(q, _, _).
.decl saqf_helper_first(hk: symbol, x: symbol, p: symbol, l: number) cross_file
saqf_helper_first(hk, x, p, l) :- saqf_helper_hit(hk, _, _, _, _), l = min l0 : { saqf_helper_hit(hk, _, _, l0, _) },
    c = min c0 : { saqf_helper_hit(hk, _, _, l, c0) }, saqf_helper_hit(hk, q, p, l, c), saqf_action(q, x, _).

// The cases, `cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/`, read as one repository: each line ending
// in `// caught` is reported, and no other line. project-list.tsx's two queries, marked `cross-lane`, are real
// violations the runner misses today: a .tsx file's imports do not reach .ts files.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "package.json" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/package.json"
    .fixture "tsconfig.json" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/tsconfig.json"
    .fixture "apps/board/package.json" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/apps/board/package.json"
    .fixture "apps/board/app/board/actions.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/apps/board/app/board/actions.ts"
    .fixture "apps/board/app/board/queries.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/apps/board/app/board/queries.ts"
    .fixture "src/app/projects/actions.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/projects/actions.ts"
    .fixture "src/app/projects/index.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/projects/index.ts"
    .fixture "src/app/projects/page.tsx" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/projects/page.tsx"
    .fixture "src/app/projects/project-list.test.tsx" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/projects/project-list.test.tsx"
    .fixture "src/app/projects/project-list.tsx" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/projects/project-list.tsx"
    .fixture "src/app/projects/queries.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/projects/queries.ts"
    .fixture "src/app/reports/actions.tsx" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/reports/actions.tsx"
    .fixture "src/app/reports/page.tsx" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/reports/page.tsx"
    .fixture "src/app/reports/report-summary.tsx" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/app/reports/report-summary.tsx"
    .fixture "src/hooks/use-prefetch-project.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/hooks/use-prefetch-project.ts"
    .fixture "src/hooks/use-project-details.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/hooks/use-project-details.ts"
    .fixture "src/hooks/use-project-total.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/hooks/use-project-total.ts"
    .fixture "src/lib/api.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/lib/api.ts"
    .fixture "src/lib/db.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/lib/db.ts"
    .fixture "src/lib/server-queries.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/lib/server-queries.ts"
    .fixture "src/store/api.ts" from "../cases/tanstack-query-practice-server-action-as-query-fn/src/store/api.ts"
    .expect _ at "src/app/projects/queries.ts":7
    .expect _ at "src/app/projects/queries.ts":14
    .expect _ at "src/app/reports/report-summary.tsx":9
    .expect _ at "src/hooks/use-prefetch-project.ts":7
    .expect _ at "src/hooks/use-project-details.ts":10
    .expect _ at "src/hooks/use-project-details.ts":18
    .expect _ at "src/hooks/use-project-total.ts":6
.end
